    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48213" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thŏlus</span></b> , i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θόλος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a dome</i>, <i>cupola</i>, <i>a rotunda</i> (syn.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fornix, testudo),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 5, 12</span></i>
			; id. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 448, 22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 4,
			7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 5</span></i>
			<i>med.</i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 6, 282</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 296</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Mart.
				2, 59, 2</span></i>. — 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">In the tholi of the temple the votive gifts
					were suspended,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 9, 408</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 1, 4, 32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Th. 2,
				734</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 1, 56</span></i>.</div>
